Current version can be seen [[Strafe|here]].
[[File:Strafe (Beta 4.8 - Beta 24.9).png|thumb|220x220px|Beta 4.8 - Beta 24.9]]

Originally costing 5G to deal 2 damage to all enemies, its price was increased to 6G in '''Alpha 3.2''', decreased back to 5G in '''Beta 2.6''' only to be returned back to 6G in '''Beta 4.3'''. '''Beta 4.6''' nerfed it further by only dealing 2 damage to all enemy monsters, so no longer the opponent.
[[File:Strafe (Beta 25.0).png|thumb|293x293px|Beta 25.0]]
'''Beta 4.8''' decreased the cost back to 5G again, but also nerfed the effect again. Now, it will do 1-2 damage to all enemy monsters. This was buffed to 1-3 damage in '''Beta 7.1'''.
[[File:Strafe (Beta 33.0).png|thumb|293x293px|Beta 33.0]]
'''Beta 10.1''' started returning it to its roots, as it now deals 2 damage to all enemy monsters like its Beta 4.6 version, but keeping it at 5G. And '''Beta 13.1''' brought it to its original version, dealing 2 damage to all enemies for 5G. '''Beta 18.1''' went a step further and lowered its cost to 4G.
[[File:Strafe (Beta 34.0).png|thumb|293x293px|Beta 34.0]]
'''Beta 25.0''' nerfed it back down a bit, as it now will only deal DMG to the opponent if they have more HP than you, giving Strafe the same treatment as [https://undercards.wikia.com/wiki/Punishment Punishment]. '''Beta 34.0''' increased its cost back to 5G. '''Beta 35.0''' reduced its cost back to 4G but removed the secondary effect.
